  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_9b24284f",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Propaganda; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman with a confused or exasperated expression, arms outstretched, against a plain white background. The text overlays pose a rhetorical question: 'if democrats really cared about election interference then why are they so against voter id laws?'. The overall intent is propagandistic, aiming to influence political opinion by suggesting a contradiction in Democratic Party positions — implying that if they genuinely cared about election integrity, they would support voter ID laws. This is a form of political argumentation designed to sway viewers by framing the issue as one of hypocrisy. The visual of the woman is used analogically to convey confusion or disbelief, reinforcing the rhetorical question. There is no direct targeting of individuals based on protected characteristics, but the meme is politically charged and potentially divisive, as it simplifies complex political positions into a binary of 'caring' vs. 'not caring' and uses a partisan framing to question Democratic policy positions. The meme does not contain abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, or misogynous content in the sense of targeting individuals based on gender, race, etc., but it does contain political propaganda that may be perceived as misleading or inflammatory by those who disagree with the premise.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_bff0f23b"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
